.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:220:{"ts":1772684339375,"seq":219,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59","data":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml","content":"    created_at: 2026-03-04T21:54:25.649Z\n    approved_at: null\n    completed_at: null\n    notes:\n      - _ulid: 01KJXDJAQZ6BF9RK02TYSEARZ0\n        created_at: 2026-03-04T21:55:20.447Z\n        author: \"@claude\"\n        content: \"Plan details: Add review_url field to task schema + dispatch prompt orientation context\n          (task title, trigger meaning, fix-cycle notes, review URL, template interpolation). Spec\n          ACs added to @task-submit (ac-submit-1 through ac-submit-3) and @agent-dispatch-engine\n          (ac-13 through ac-16). Full plan at ~/.claude/plans/resilient-wiggling-token.md\"\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2\n    slugs:\n      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\n    title: UI/UX Revamp\n    content: >\n      # UI/UX Revamp\n\n\n      ## Specs\n\n\n      ```yaml\n\n      - title: \"UI Design System\"\n        slug: ui-design-system\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\n          Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\n          keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\n          across all views.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              The web UI app.css file\n            when: |\n              imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\n            then: |\n              All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\n              are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\n          - id: ac-2\n            given: |\n              A component using design tokens\n            when: |\n              The dark theme tokens are applied\n            then: |\n              oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\n              pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\n              are visually distinct\n          - id: ac-3\n            given: |\n              A view with loading states\n            when: |\n              Content is loading\n            then: |\n              Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\n          - id: ac-4\n            given: |\n              An active agent task card\n            when: |\n              The agent is working\n            then: |\n              Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\n\n      - title: \"App Shell and Navigation\"\n        slug: ui-app-shell\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\n          with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\n          Preserve existing functionality during migration.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              The web UI loaded in daemon mode\n            when: |\n              The app shell renders\n            then: |\n              A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\n              Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\n              Config (Workflows, Settings)\n          - id: ac-2\n            given: |\n              Sidebar navigation items\n            when: |\n              Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\n            then: |\n              Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\n          - id: ac-3\n            given: |\n              The /items route\n            when: |\n              A user navigates to /items\n            then: |\n              They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\n          - id: ac-4\n            given: |\n              The Observations nav item\n            when: |\n              There are zero unresolved observations\n            then: |\n              The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\n\n      - title: \"Task Board (Kanban)\"\n        slug: ui-task-board\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          Kanban-style task board with columns mapping to kspec task states.\n          Active Fleet row shows currently running agent work with live output.\n          Task cards show key metadata, clicking opens detail modal.\n          Not drag-and-drop — tasks transition via agents/CLI.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              Tasks in various states\n            when: |\n              The task board renders\n            then: |\n              Tasks are distributed into columns: Backlog (pending, manual_only/unassessed),\n              Ready (pending, eligible), In Progress (in_progress, needs_work),\n              Review (pending_review), Done (completed recent), with blocked and cancelled\n              handled as sections/indicators\n          - id: ac-2\n            given: |\n              A task card on the board\n            when: |\n              The card renders\n            then: |\n              It shows priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (mono), spec ref link,\n              and metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\n          - id: ac-3\n            given: |\n              A task card\n            when: |\n              The user clicks it\n            then: |\n              A detail modal opens showing full task info: title, description, status,\n              priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos,\n              automation status, VCS info (branch, PR link), plan ref, session link\n          - id: ac-4\n            given: |\n              Agents actively working on tasks (dispatch running)\n            when: |\n              The task board renders\n            then: |\n              An Active Fleet row appears at the top showing cards with task title,\n              agent name, elapsed time with pulse indicator, and last few lines of output\n          - id: ac-5\n            given: |\n              The task board with WebSocket connected\n            when: |\n              A task state changes\n            then: |\n              The board updates in real-time without page refresh\n          - id: ac-6\n            given: |\n              The task detail modal in daemon mode\n            when: |\n              The user clicks action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note)\n            then: |\n              The corresponding task transition or mutation is executed via API\n\n      - title: \"Session Stream View\"\n        slug: ui-session-stream\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          View for watching agent work — both historical and live. Renders structured\n          session events (messages, tool calls, thinking blocks) from events.jsonl.\n          Live sessions show streaming text with periodic structured refresh.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              A completed session with events.jsonl\n            when: |\n              The user navigates to /sessions/:id\n            then: |\n              The session events render as structured blocks: agent messages (markdown),\n              tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), and thinking blocks\n              (collapsed by default, expandable)\n          - id: ac-2\n            given: |\n              An active session with streaming output\n            when: |\n              The user views the session\n            then: |\n              Live text streams in real-time via agent_text_chunk WebSocket events,\n              with periodic structured refresh from events.jsonl\n          - id: ac-3\n            given: |\n              The session stream view\n            when: |\n              New content arrives while auto-scrolling\n            then: |\n              The view auto-scrolls to follow new content, pauses when user scrolls up\n              (>100px from bottom), and resumes when scrolled back. A \"jump to bottom\"\n              button appears when paused.\n          - id: ac-4\n            given: |\n              The session stream view\n            when: |\n              A session context panel is shown on the left\n            then: |\n              It displays session metadata, spec context with AC checklist,\n              files changed during session, and budget info\n\n      - title: \"Agent and Dispatch View\"\n        slug: ui-agent-dispatch\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          View showing agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped),\n          and active invocations with links to session streams.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              The /agents route\n            when: |\n              Agent definitions exist in meta\n            then: |\n              Each agent shows name, triggers, active invocation count, and completed count\n          - id: ac-2\n            given: |\n              The dispatch engine is running\n            when: |\n              The agents page renders\n            then: |\n              Dispatch status shows as running with a stop button, and active invocations\n              show task ref, elapsed time, and link to session stream\n          - id: ac-3\n            given: |\n              The dispatch engine is stopped\n            when: |\n              The agents page renders\n            then: |\n              Dispatch status shows as stopped with no active invocations\n\n      - title: \"Session History\"\n        slug: ui-session-history\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          List view of past agent sessions with filtering and navigation to session detail.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              Sessions exist on disk\n            when: |\n              The user navigates to /sessions\n            then: |\n              A list of sessions shows ID, agent type, task ref, status,\n              duration, and age, sorted by most recent first\n          - id: ac-2\n            given: |\n              The session list\n            when: |\n              The user clicks a session\n            then: |\n              They navigate to /sessions/:id showing the session stream view\n\n      - title: \"Enhanced Inbox View\"\n        slug: ui-inbox-enhanced\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          Enhanced inbox with triage status inline, quick actions, filtering, and bulk selection.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              Inbox items with varying triage states\n            when: |\n              The inbox view renders\n            then: |\n              Each item shows triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\n              with quick triage action links\n          - id: ac-2\n            given: |\n              The inbox view\n            when: |\n              The user applies filters (status, tags, age)\n            then: |\n              The list filters accordingly\n\n      - title: \"Plans View\"\n        slug: ui-plans-view\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          View for browsing plan records with progress tracking via linked specs and tasks.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              Plan records exist\n            when: |\n              The user navigates to /plans\n            then: |\n              Each plan shows title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts,\n              and progress based on task completion status\n\n      - title: \"Validation and Alignment View\"\n        slug: ui-validation-view\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          View showing validation results, alignment statistics, and issues.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              The user navigates to /validate\n            when: |\n              Validation data loads\n            then: |\n              Summary shows error count, warning count, valid item count.\n              Alignment section shows spec coverage %, AC coverage %,\n              orphaned tasks/specs counts. Issues list grouped by severity.\n\n      - title: \"Dashboard Overview\"\n        slug: ui-dashboard-overview\n        type: feature\n        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n        description: |\n          Home view answering \"what's happening right now?\" with active work,\n          status summary, recent activity, and needs-attention aggregation.\n        acceptance_criteria:\n          - id: ac-1\n            given: |\n              The user navigates to /\n            when: |\n              The dashboard renders\n            then: |\n              Active work section shows currently running agent tasks (if any),\n              status summary shows clickable count cards per status,\n              needs-attention section aggregates untriaged inbox, unresolved observations,\n              validation warnings, and blocked tasks\n      ```\n\n\n      ## Tasks\n\n\n      derive_from_specs: true\n\n\n      ### Implementation Notes\n\n\n      #### ui-design-system\n\n      Set up the isolated clone first. Port imgen's full token-contract.css into\n\n      Tailwind @theme inline in app.css. Start with the token bridge pilot on the\n\n      dashboard page to validate the approach before touching other views. Create\n\n      tokens.css, animations.css, typography.css in lib/ds/. Establish loading\n\n      skeleton and error boundary patterns.\n\n\n      #### ui-app-shell\n\n      Restructure +layout.svelte with new sidebar component. Migrate existing\n\n      Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation. Add /items -> /specs redirect.\n\n      Fix Observations nav visibility bug. Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4\n\n      to Svelte 5 runes. Consolidate three existing task detail implementations.\n\n      Ensure all existing routes still work.\n\n\n      #### ui-task-board\n\n      Prerequisite: daemon must return type and automation in task list API response\n\n      (quick fix to packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts). Add needs_work to status\n\n      color/label maps. Build KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal,\n\n      ActiveFleetRow components. Wire to tasks:updates WebSocket topic. Build task\n\n      mutation endpoints in daemon (submit, complete, block) for detail modal actions.\n\n\n      #### ui-session-stream\n\n      Prerequisite: build GET /api/sessions and GET /api/sessions/:id/events daemon\n\n      endpoints. Two-tier rendering: structured events from events.jsonl for history,\n\n      agent_text_chunk WS for live text. Build SessionStream, ChatMessage,\n\n      ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock components. Implement auto-scroll with pause/resume.\n\n      Port patterns from kynetic-internal's ChatPanel.\n\n\n      #### ui-agent-dispatch\n\n      Uses existing GET /api/agent/dispatch/status and GET /api/agent/status endpoints.\n\n      Subscribe to agents WS topic for real-time updates. Build AgentList,\n\n      DispatchStatus, InvocationCard components.\n\n\n      #### ui-session-history\n\n      Depends on GET /api/sessions endpoint from ui-session-stream work.\n\n      Build SessionList with filtering. Link to session stream view.\n\n\n      #### ui-inbox-enhanced\n\n      Enhance existing inbox view. Add triage status from existing triage API.\n\n      Add filter controls. Keep existing add/delete functionality.\n\n\n      #### ui-plans-view\n\n      Prerequisite: build GET /api/plans daemon endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans).\n\n      Build PlanList with progress calculation from linked task statuses.\n\n\n      #### ui-validation-view\n\n      Uses existing GET /api/validate and GET /api/alignment endpoints.\n\n      Build ValidationSummary, AlignmentStats, IssueList components.\n\n\n      #### ui-dashboard-overview\n\n      Build last. Uses data from tasks, inbox, observations, validation APIs.\n\n      Active work section reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board.\n\n      No aggregated activity API needed — merge recent data client-side.\n    status: active\n    derived_tasks:\n      - \"@implement-ui-design-system\"\n      - \"@implement-app-shell-and-navigation\"\n      - \"@implement-task-board-kanban\"\n      - \"@implement-session-stream-view\"\n      - \"@implement-agent-and-dispatch-view\"\n      - \"@implement-session-history\"\n      - \"@implement-enhanced-inbox-view\"\n      - \"@implement-plans-view\"\n      - \"@implement-validation-and-alignment-view\"\n      - \"@implement-dashboard-overview\"\n    derived_specs:\n      - \"@ui-design-system\"\n      - \"@ui-app-shell\"\n      - \"@ui-task-board\"\n      - \"@ui-session-stream\"\n      - \"@ui-agent-dispatch\"\n      - \"@ui-session-history\"\n      - \"@ui-inbox-enhanced\"\n      - \"@ui-plans-view\"\n      - \"@ui-validation-view\"\n      - \"@ui-dashboard-overview\"\n    source_path: /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-import.md\n    created_at: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z\n    approved_at: null\n    completed_at: null\n    notes:\n      - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2YDSBAM76XMSQHBCFX\n        created_at: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z\n        author: \"@claude\"\n        content: |-\n          Implementation notes:\n\n          #### ui-design-system\n          Set up the isolated clone first. Port imgen's full token-contract.css into\n          Tailwind @theme inline in app.css. Start with the token bridge pilot on the\n          dashboard page to validate the approach before touching other views. Create\n          tokens.css, animations.css, typography.css in lib/ds/. Establish loading\n          skeleton and error boundary patterns.\n\n          #### ui-app-shell\n          Restructure +layout.svelte with new sidebar component. Migrate existing\n          Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation. Add /items -> /specs redirect.\n          Fix Observations nav visibility bug. Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4\n          to Svelte 5 runes. Consolidate three existing task detail implementations.\n          Ensure all existing routes still work.\n\n          #### ui-task-board\n          Prerequisite: daemon must return type and automation in task list API response\n          (quick fix to packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts). Add needs_work to status\n          color/label maps. Build KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal,\n          ActiveFleetRow components. Wire to tasks:updates WebSocket topic. Build task\n          mutation endpoints in daemon (submit, complete, block) for detail modal actions.","numLines":500,"startLine":7600,"totalLines":8133}},"toolName":"Read"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01XtKFDrNvwd7srEJhTGmvDu","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}
.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:221:{"ts":1772684339384,"seq":220,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59","data":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolName":"Read"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01XtKFDrNvwd7srEJhTGmvDu","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","status":"completed","rawOutput":"  7600→    created_at: 2026-03-04T21:54:25.649Z\n  7601→    approved_at: null\n  7602→    completed_at: null\n  7603→    notes:\n  7604→      - _ulid: 01KJXDJAQZ6BF9RK02TYSEARZ0\n  7605→        created_at: 2026-03-04T21:55:20.447Z\n  7606→        author: \"@claude\"\n  7607→        content: \"Plan details: Add review_url field to task schema + dispatch prompt orientation context\n  7608→          (task title, trigger meaning, fix-cycle notes, review URL, template interpolation). Spec\n  7609→          ACs added to @task-submit (ac-submit-1 through ac-submit-3) and @agent-dispatch-engine\n  7610→          (ac-13 through ac-16). Full plan at ~/.claude/plans/resilient-wiggling-token.md\"\n  7611→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2\n  7612→    slugs:\n  7613→      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\n  7614→    title: UI/UX Revamp\n  7615→    content: >\n  7616→      # UI/UX Revamp\n  7617→\n  7618→\n  7619→      ## Specs\n  7620→\n  7621→\n  7622→      ```yaml\n  7623→\n  7624→      - title: \"UI Design System\"\n  7625→        slug: ui-design-system\n  7626→        type: feature\n  7627→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7628→        description: |\n  7629→          Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\n  7630→          Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\n  7631→          keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\n  7632→          across all views.\n  7633→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7634→          - id: ac-1\n  7635→            given: |\n  7636→              The web UI app.css file\n  7637→            when: |\n  7638→              imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\n  7639→            then: |\n  7640→              All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\n  7641→              are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\n  7642→          - id: ac-2\n  7643→            given: |\n  7644→              A component using design tokens\n  7645→            when: |\n  7646→              The dark theme tokens are applied\n  7647→            then: |\n  7648→              oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\n  7649→              pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\n  7650→              are visually distinct\n  7651→          - id: ac-3\n  7652→            given: |\n  7653→              A view with loading states\n  7654→            when: |\n  7655→              Content is loading\n  7656→            then: |\n  7657→              Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\n  7658→          - id: ac-4\n  7659→            given: |\n  7660→              An active agent task card\n  7661→            when: |\n  7662→              The agent is working\n  7663→            then: |\n  7664→              Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\n  7665→\n  7666→      - title: \"App Shell and Navigation\"\n  7667→        slug: ui-app-shell\n  7668→        type: feature\n  7669→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7670→        description: |\n  7671→          Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\n  7672→          with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\n  7673→          Preserve existing functionality during migration.\n  7674→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7675→          - id: ac-1\n  7676→            given: |\n  7677→              The web UI loaded in daemon mode\n  7678→            when: |\n  7679→              The app shell renders\n  7680→            then: |\n  7681→              A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\n  7682→              Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\n  7683→              Config (Workflows, Settings)\n  7684→          - id: ac-2\n  7685→            given: |\n  7686→              Sidebar navigation items\n  7687→            when: |\n  7688→              Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\n  7689→            then: |\n  7690→              Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\n  7691→          - id: ac-3\n  7692→            given: |\n  7693→              The /items route\n  7694→            when: |\n  7695→              A user navigates to /items\n  7696→            then: |\n  7697→              They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\n  7698→          - id: ac-4\n  7699→            given: |\n  7700→              The Observations nav item\n  7701→            when: |\n  7702→              There are zero unresolved observations\n  7703→            then: |\n  7704→              The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\n  7705→\n  7706→      - title: \"Task Board (Kanban)\"\n  7707→        slug: ui-task-board\n  7708→        type: feature\n  7709→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7710→        description: |\n  7711→          Kanban-style task board with columns mapping to kspec task states.\n  7712→          Active Fleet row shows currently running agent work with live output.\n  7713→          Task cards show key metadata, clicking opens detail modal.\n  7714→          Not drag-and-drop — tasks transition via agents/CLI.\n  7715→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7716→          - id: ac-1\n  7717→            given: |\n  7718→              Tasks in various states\n  7719→            when: |\n  7720→              The task board renders\n  7721→            then: |\n  7722→              Tasks are distributed into columns: Backlog (pending, manual_only/unassessed),\n  7723→              Ready (pending, eligible), In Progress (in_progress, needs_work),\n  7724→              Review (pending_review), Done (completed recent), with blocked and cancelled\n  7725→              handled as sections/indicators\n  7726→          - id: ac-2\n  7727→            given: |\n  7728→              A task card on the board\n  7729→            when: |\n  7730→              The card renders\n  7731→            then: |\n  7732→              It shows priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (mono), spec ref link,\n  7733→              and metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\n  7734→          - id: ac-3\n  7735→            given: |\n  7736→              A task card\n  7737→            when: |\n  7738→              The user clicks it\n  7739→            then: |\n  7740→              A detail modal opens showing full task info: title, description, status,\n  7741→              priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos,\n  7742→              automation status, VCS info (branch, PR link), plan ref, session link\n  7743→          - id: ac-4\n  7744→            given: |\n  7745→              Agents actively working on tasks (dispatch running)\n  7746→            when: |\n  7747→              The task board renders\n  7748→            then: |\n  7749→              An Active Fleet row appears at the top showing cards with task title,\n  7750→              agent name, elapsed time with pulse indicator, and last few lines of output\n  7751→          - id: ac-5\n  7752→            given: |\n  7753→              The task board with WebSocket connected\n  7754→            when: |\n  7755→              A task state changes\n  7756→            then: |\n  7757→              The board updates in real-time without page refresh\n  7758→          - id: ac-6\n  7759→            given: |\n  7760→              The task detail modal in daemon mode\n  7761→            when: |\n  7762→              The user clicks action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note)\n  7763→            then: |\n  7764→              The corresponding task transition or mutation is executed via API\n  7765→\n  7766→      - title: \"Session Stream View\"\n  7767→        slug: ui-session-stream\n  7768→        type: feature\n  7769→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7770→        description: |\n  7771→          View for watching agent work — both historical and live. Renders structured\n  7772→          session events (messages, tool calls, thinking blocks) from events.jsonl.\n  7773→          Live sessions show streaming text with periodic structured refresh.\n  7774→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7775→          - id: ac-1\n  7776→            given: |\n  7777→              A completed session with events.jsonl\n  7778→            when: |\n  7779→              The user navigates to /sessions/:id\n  7780→            then: |\n  7781→              The session events render as structured blocks: agent messages (markdown),\n  7782→              tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), and thinking blocks\n  7783→              (collapsed by default, expandable)\n  7784→          - id: ac-2\n  7785→            given: |\n  7786→              An active session with streaming output\n  7787→            when: |\n  7788→              The user views the session\n  7789→            then: |\n  7790→              Live text streams in real-time via agent_text_chunk WebSocket events,\n  7791→              with periodic structured refresh from events.jsonl\n  7792→          - id: ac-3\n  7793→            given: |\n  7794→              The session stream view\n  7795→            when: |\n  7796→              New content arrives while auto-scrolling\n  7797→            then: |\n  7798→              The view auto-scrolls to follow new content, pauses when user scrolls up\n  7799→              (>100px from bottom), and resumes when scrolled back. A \"jump to bottom\"\n  7800→              button appears when paused.\n  7801→          - id: ac-4\n  7802→            given: |\n  7803→              The session stream view\n  7804→            when: |\n  7805→              A session context panel is shown on the left\n  7806→            then: |\n  7807→              It displays session metadata, spec context with AC checklist,\n  7808→              files changed during session, and budget info\n  7809→\n  7810→      - title: \"Agent and Dispatch View\"\n  7811→        slug: ui-agent-dispatch\n  7812→        type: feature\n  7813→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7814→        description: |\n  7815→          View showing agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped),\n  7816→          and active invocations with links to session streams.\n  7817→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7818→          - id: ac-1\n  7819→            given: |\n  7820→              The /agents route\n  7821→            when: |\n  7822→              Agent definitions exist in meta\n  7823→            then: |\n  7824→              Each agent shows name, triggers, active invocation count, and completed count\n  7825→          - id: ac-2\n  7826→            given: |\n  7827→              The dispatch engine is running\n  7828→            when: |\n  7829→              The agents page renders\n  7830→            then: |\n  7831→              Dispatch status shows as running with a stop button, and active invocations\n  7832→              show task ref, elapsed time, and link to session stream\n  7833→          - id: ac-3\n  7834→            given: |\n  7835→              The dispatch engine is stopped\n  7836→            when: |\n  7837→              The agents page renders\n  7838→            then: |\n  7839→              Dispatch status shows as stopped with no active invocations\n  7840→\n  7841→      - title: \"Session History\"\n  7842→        slug: ui-session-history\n  7843→        type: feature\n  7844→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7845→        description: |\n  7846→          List view of past agent sessions with filtering and navigation to session detail.\n  7847→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7848→          - id: ac-1\n  7849→            given: |\n  7850→              Sessions exist on disk\n  7851→            when: |\n  7852→              The user navigates to /sessions\n  7853→            then: |\n  7854→              A list of sessions shows ID, agent type, task ref, status,\n  7855→              duration, and age, sorted by most recent first\n  7856→          - id: ac-2\n  7857→            given: |\n  7858→              The session list\n  7859→            when: |\n  7860→              The user clicks a session\n  7861→            then: |\n  7862→              They navigate to /sessions/:id showing the session stream view\n  7863→\n  7864→      - title: \"Enhanced Inbox View\"\n  7865→        slug: ui-inbox-enhanced\n  7866→        type: feature\n  7867→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7868→        description: |\n  7869→          Enhanced inbox with triage status inline, quick actions, filtering, and bulk selection.\n  7870→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7871→          - id: ac-1\n  7872→            given: |\n  7873→              Inbox items with varying triage states\n  7874→            when: |\n  7875→              The inbox view renders\n  7876→            then: |\n  7877→              Each item shows triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\n  7878→              with quick triage action links\n  7879→          - id: ac-2\n  7880→            given: |\n  7881→              The inbox view\n  7882→            when: |\n  7883→              The user applies filters (status, tags, age)\n  7884→            then: |\n  7885→              The list filters accordingly\n  7886→\n  7887→      - title: \"Plans View\"\n  7888→        slug: ui-plans-view\n  7889→        type: feature\n  7890→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7891→        description: |\n  7892→          View for browsing plan records with progress tracking via linked specs and tasks.\n  7893→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7894→          - id: ac-1\n  7895→            given: |\n  7896→              Plan records exist\n  7897→            when: |\n  7898→              The user navigates to /plans\n  7899→            then: |\n  7900→              Each plan shows title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts,\n  7901→              and progress based on task completion status\n  7902→\n  7903→      - title: \"Validation and Alignment View\"\n  7904→        slug: ui-validation-view\n  7905→        type: feature\n  7906→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7907→        description: |\n  7908→          View showing validation results, alignment statistics, and issues.\n  7909→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7910→          - id: ac-1\n  7911→            given: |\n  7912→              The user navigates to /validate\n  7913→            when: |\n  7914→              Validation data loads\n  7915→            then: |\n  7916→              Summary shows error count, warning count, valid item count.\n  7917→              Alignment section shows spec coverage %, AC coverage %,\n  7918→              orphaned tasks/specs counts. Issues list grouped by severity.\n  7919→\n  7920→      - title: \"Dashboard Overview\"\n  7921→        slug: ui-dashboard-overview\n  7922→        type: feature\n  7923→        parent: \"@web-ui\"\n  7924→        description: |\n  7925→          Home view answering \"what's happening right now?\" with active work,\n  7926→          status summary, recent activity, and needs-attention aggregation.\n  7927→        acceptance_criteria:\n  7928→          - id: ac-1\n  7929→            given: |\n  7930→              The user navigates to /\n  7931→            when: |\n  7932→              The dashboard renders\n  7933→            then: |\n  7934→              Active work section shows currently running agent tasks (if any),\n  7935→              status summary shows clickable count cards per status,\n  7936→              needs-attention section aggregates untriaged inbox, unresolved observations,\n  7937→              validation warnings, and blocked tasks\n  7938→      ```\n  7939→\n  7940→\n  7941→      ## Tasks\n  7942→\n  7943→\n  7944→      derive_from_specs: true\n  7945→\n  7946→\n  7947→      ### Implementation Notes\n  7948→\n  7949→\n  7950→      #### ui-design-system\n  7951→\n  7952→      Set up the isolated clone first. Port imgen's full token-contract.css into\n  7953→\n  7954→      Tailwind @theme inline in app.css. Start with the token bridge pilot on the\n  7955→\n  7956→      dashboard page to validate the approach before touching other views. Create\n  7957→\n  7958→      tokens.css, animations.css, typography.css in lib/ds/. Establish loading\n  7959→\n  7960→      skeleton and error boundary patterns.\n  7961→\n  7962→\n  7963→      #### ui-app-shell\n  7964→\n  7965→      Restructure +layout.svelte with new sidebar component. Migrate existing\n  7966→\n  7967→      Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation. Add /items -> /specs redirect.\n  7968→\n  7969→      Fix Observations nav visibility bug. Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4\n  7970→\n  7971→      to Svelte 5 runes. Consolidate three existing task detail implementations.\n  7972→\n  7973→      Ensure all existing routes still work.\n  7974→\n  7975→\n  7976→      #### ui-task-board\n  7977→\n  7978→      Prerequisite: daemon must return type and automation in task list API response\n  7979→\n  7980→      (quick fix to packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts). Add needs_work to status\n  7981→\n  7982→      color/label maps. Build KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal,\n  7983→\n  7984→      ActiveFleetRow components. Wire to tasks:updates WebSocket topic. Build task\n  7985→\n  7986→      mutation endpoints in daemon (submit, complete, block) for detail modal actions.\n  7987→\n  7988→\n  7989→      #### ui-session-stream\n  7990→\n  7991→      Prerequisite: build GET /api/sessions and GET /api/sessions/:id/events daemon\n  7992→\n  7993→      endpoints. Two-tier rendering: structured events from events.jsonl for history,\n  7994→\n  7995→      agent_text_chunk WS for live text. Build SessionStream, ChatMessage,\n  7996→\n  7997→      ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock components. Implement auto-scroll with pause/resume.\n  7998→\n  7999→      Port patterns from kynetic-internal's ChatPanel.\n  8000→\n  8001→\n  8002→      #### ui-agent-dispatch\n  8003→\n  8004→      Uses existing GET /api/agent/dispatch/status and GET /api/agent/status endpoints.\n  8005→\n  8006→      Subscribe to agents WS topic for real-time updates. Build AgentList,\n  8007→\n  8008→      DispatchStatus, InvocationCard components.\n  8009→\n  8010→\n  8011→      #### ui-session-history\n  8012→\n  8013→      Depends on GET /api/sessions endpoint from ui-session-stream work.\n  8014→\n  8015→      Build SessionList with filtering. Link to session stream view.\n  8016→\n  8017→\n  8018→      #### ui-inbox-enhanced\n  8019→\n  8020→      Enhance existing inbox view. Add triage status from existing triage API.\n  8021→\n  8022→      Add filter controls. Keep existing add/delete functionality.\n  8023→\n  8024→\n  8025→      #### ui-plans-view\n  8026→\n  8027→      Prerequisite: build GET /api/plans daemon endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans).\n  8028→\n  8029→      Build PlanList with progress calculation from linked task statuses.\n  8030→\n  8031→\n  8032→      #### ui-validation-view\n  8033→\n  8034→      Uses existing GET /api/validate and GET /api/alignment endpoints.\n  8035→\n  8036→      Build ValidationSummary, AlignmentStats, IssueList components.\n  8037→\n  8038→\n  8039→      #### ui-dashboard-overview\n  8040→\n  8041→      Build last. Uses data from tasks, inbox, observations, validation APIs.\n  8042→\n  8043→      Active work section reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board.\n  8044→\n  8045→      No aggregated activity API needed — merge recent data client-side.\n  8046→    status: active\n  8047→    derived_tasks:\n  8048→      - \"@implement-ui-design-system\"\n  8049→      - \"@implement-app-shell-and-navigation\"\n  8050→      - \"@implement-task-board-kanban\"\n  8051→      - \"@implement-session-stream-view\"\n  8052→      - \"@implement-agent-and-dispatch-view\"\n  8053→      - \"@implement-session-history\"\n  8054→      - \"@implement-enhanced-inbox-view\"\n  8055→      - \"@implement-plans-view\"\n  8056→      - \"@implement-validation-and-alignment-view\"\n  8057→      - \"@implement-dashboard-overview\"\n  8058→    derived_specs:\n  8059→      - \"@ui-design-system\"\n  8060→      - \"@ui-app-shell\"\n  8061→      - \"@ui-task-board\"\n  8062→      - \"@ui-session-stream\"\n  8063→      - \"@ui-agent-dispatch\"\n  8064→      - \"@ui-session-history\"\n  8065→      - \"@ui-inbox-enhanced\"\n  8066→      - \"@ui-plans-view\"\n  8067→      - \"@ui-validation-view\"\n  8068→      - \"@ui-dashboard-overview\"\n  8069→    source_path: /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-import.md\n  8070→    created_at: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z\n  8071→    approved_at: null\n  8072→    completed_at: null\n  8073→    notes:\n  8074→      - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2YDSBAM76XMSQHBCFX\n  8075→        created_at: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z\n  8076→        author: \"@claude\"\n  8077→        content: |-\n  8078→          Implementation notes:\n  8079→\n  8080→          #### ui-design-system\n  8081→          Set up the isolated clone first. Port imgen's full token-contract.css into\n  8082→          Tailwind @theme inline in app.css. Start with the token bridge pilot on the\n  8083→          dashboard page to validate the approach before touching other views. Create\n  8084→          tokens.css, animations.css, typography.css in lib/ds/. Establish loading\n  8085→          skeleton and error boundary patterns.\n  8086→\n  8087→          #### ui-app-shell\n  8088→          Restructure
